mpare the cited file's current sha256 ...). File-level in v1; line-level ... is a deferred follow-on (ADR 0037).'","region_for_finding returns REGION_CHANGED when the WHOLE file hash differs, not the cited line/region — so an edit at a.py:200 marks a finding at a.py:40 as CHANGED.","Motivating bug: on 1867 the 'assert elapsed < 10' advisory survived PS3-PS4; if those patchsets touched the same file at all, the addressed classifier would drop rather than carry it."],"finding":"The 'addressed' classifier (REGION_CHANGED -> not carried) uses region_gate.region_for_finding, which is FILE-LEVEL in v1, as a proxy for 'the finding was acted on'; any unrelated edit elsewhere in the cited file flips it to REGION_CHANGED and silently drops a still-present finding — the opposite fail direction from the floor's fail-safe use, and it can reproduce the motivating 1867 miss (a defect surviving across patchsets that also edited its file).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa699e6323ea3dc0f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach -> 'State — one rule per value' (addressed = REGION_CHANGED) and region_gate.py:9-12 (file-level in v1; line-level deferred, ADR 0037)","norm_id":"nd488ac656fd0f1b8","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A finding at a.py:40 that PS(k+1) does not re-emit while PS(k+1) edits a.py at an unrelated line -> REGION_CHANGED -> classified 'addressed' -> dropped, never injected, even though the defect line is byte-identical.","The exact 1867 pattern: a persistent defect on a file that keeps receiving unrelated edits patchset-to-patchset never carries forward."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Decide 'addressed' from the fresh Pass-1 finder's signal at the cited location (finder silent AND the region actually changed at line granularity) rather than a whole-file content hash; alternatively default an unresolvable/coarse REGION_CHANGED to 'still-present' (carry) so file-level churn cannot silently drop a f